    "narrative": "Luarca is a small fishing town tucked into a deep natural harbour. The Capilla de la Atalaya (16th-century watchtower chapel) and the town cemetery sit on the clifftop above the harbour — the cemetery holds the grave of Severo Ochoa, the Luarca-born Nobel laureate in physiology (1959). The town is known as 'the white village of the Green Coast' for its whitewashed fishermen's houses climbing up from the harbour. The pilgrim accommodation is good.",
